# Oracle samples, round r10 (2026-11-02).
# Format: BRANCH | ID | WHAT IT PROBES -> OUTPUT THAT CONFIRMS IT | SCRIPT
# SCRIPT is one batch file; "\n" separates its lines (written with CRLF). Run as a .bat file.
B | O1 | does the child cmd split at ^& after a block -> a CHILDSPLIT line if it splits | @cmd /c (ver ^>nul) ^^^& echo CHILDSPLIT
B | O1b | same, setting a variable in the child -> R10A is not set in the parent either way; stderr shows whether the child ran set | @cmd /c (ver ^>nul) ^^^& set R10A=1\n@set R10A
B | O2 | FOR /F command string with an escaped ) after nul -> [CHILDSPLIT] if the child splits | @for /f "delims=" %%a in ('(ver ^>nul^) ^^^& echo CHILDSPLIT') do @echo [%%a]
B | O3 | FOR /F command string with an unescaped ) after nul -> [CHILDSPLIT] if the child splits | @for /f "delims=" %%a in ('(ver ^>nul) ^^^& echo CHILDSPLIT') do @echo [%%a]
A | G1 | caret before the GOTO label colon -> END alone if the caret is removed | @echo off\ngoto ^:end\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
A | G2 | equals sign after a GOTO label -> END alone if = ends the label | @echo off\ngoto :end=x\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
A | G3 | semicolon after a CALL label -> SUB, then BACK | @echo off\ncall :sub;x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:sub\necho SUB\nexit /b
A | G4 | equals sign after a CALL label -> SUB, then BACK | @echo off\ncall :sub=x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:sub\necho SUB\nexit /b
A | G5 | plus after a CALL label -> SUB, then BACK if + ends the label | @echo off\ncall :sub+x\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:sub\necho SUB\nexit /b
A | G6 | CALL with a double colon -> SUB, then BACK if one colon is stripped | @echo off\ncall ::sub\necho BACK\nexit /b\n:sub\necho SUB\nexit /b
A | G7 | colon after a GOTO label -> END alone if : ends the label | @echo off\ngoto :end:x\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
A | G8 | GOTO ::show with both ::show and :show labels -> COLONCOLON or SHOW names the label taken | @echo off\ngoto ::show\necho FELL\nexit /b\n::show\necho COLONCOLON\nexit /b\n:show\necho SHOW
A | G9 | caret inside the GOTO keyword -> END alone if go^to is goto | @echo off\ngo^to :end\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
A | G10 | caret inside a GOTO label -> END alone if the caret is removed | @echo off\ngoto :e^nd\necho FELL\n:end\necho END
